lore_blurb = "First-generation cortical interface recovered from Hangar 4B during the 1979 Facility Expansion. Construction method unknown. No solder points. No discrete components. The circuit geometry, if it can be called that, is grown rather than manufactured — branching structures 40 nanometers across that respond to electrical stimulus by reconfiguring themselves.\n\nThe signal it broadcasts on 14.7 MHz does not match any known communications protocol. Our best analysis suggests it is not transmitting data. It is transmitting pattern. The AI Oversight system began logging the signal 72 hours before we identified it ourselves."
